      },
      {
         "IntroSequence": {
            "SequenceItems": [
               {
                  "Type": "SlideShow",
                  "Data": {
                     "SlideImageSequence": "textures/campaign/glory_of_greece/7/intro/%d.png",
                     "Slides": [
                        {
                           "Duration": 45.0,
                           "TextFadeDuration": 44.8,
                           "FadeInTime": 0.2,
                           "FadeOutTime": 0.2,
                           "String": "Mesopotamia, 401 BCE\n\nThe Peloponnesian War has concluded, bringing peace to Hellas for a short time. You are part of a company of 10,000 Greek mercenaries hired to support Cyrus the Younger in his struggle to claim the Persian throne from Artaxerxes II, his brother. The Battle of Cunaxa yielded an overwhelming victory for your company, but it is all for naught as Cyrus fell in combat. Your contingent of mercenaries is now isolated deep inside the Persian Empire, with no help in sight. The journey to the nearest port on the Black Sea will be long and perilous, but it yields the opportunity for ample spoils and an eventual return home. Capture the Artifact held in the city on the coast, build a transport ship there, and bring the Artifact to friendly territory in the far north.",
                           "ImageRect": {
                              "x": 0,
                              "y": 0,
                              "width": 3840,
                              "height": 2160
                           },
                           "TextRect": {
                              "x": 230,
